# Line endings, pinned deliberately.
#
# Shell hooks MUST be LF. This machine has core.autocrlf=true, so without this rule a fresh checkout
# gets "#!/bin/sh\r" and every hook dies with "bad interpreter" before it can run - which is the worst
# possible failure for a gate: silent, on someone else's machine, and looks like the repo is broken.
.githooks/* text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# PowerShell scripts are left at the repo's current default (autocrlf). PS 5.1 reads LF happily, so
# there is no correctness reason to churn every existing .ps1's working-tree ending; what actually
# bites those files is *encoding* (BOM-less UTF-8 is read as ANSI), so keep .ps1 content ASCII.

# Windows XML/props keep their CRLF expectations alone - MSBuild does not care, and churn there
# pollutes diffs for no reason.
* text=auto
